<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 147 0 R
/T (Hiring teams get flooded with applications, so most rely on automated screening software to shortlist candidates. These tools scan resumes for the exact terms listed in a job posting and rank people by how many they hit.)
/E (Hiring teams get flooded with applications, so most rely on automated screening software to shortlist candidates. These tools scan resumes for the exact terms listed in a job posting and rank people by how many they hit.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
198 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 147 0 R
/E (Literal word matching can't tell when two phrases describe the same ability. Someone who "managed a group of five interns" may score low for a role asking for "leadership experience," simply because the wording differs. Capable applicants get overlooked, and employers lose out on people who would have been a good fit.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
