207 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (This project aims to build a screening tool that judges how well a resume fits a job posting by what the text means, not which words it happens to use. The goal is to recognize equivalent skills phrased differently, give qualified candidates a fairer shot, and help recruiters surface the right people faster)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 148 0 R
/E (A pre-trained language model such as Sentence-BERT turns both the resume and the job description into numerical embeddings that capture meaning. The two embeddings are then compared using cosine similarity to produce a match score. To check the benefit, results are compared against a standard keyword-matching baseline.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
